            controls the motor's torque?
            A) Voltage across the terminals.
            B) Current through the armature coils.  ← CORRECT
            C) The PWM frequency.
            D) The resistance of the motor windings.

        Q2. Why can't a GPIO pin drive a DC motor directly?
            A) GPIO pins can only output 1.8 V, which is too low for any motor.
            B) GPIO pins are AC outputs and motors require DC.
            C) GPIO pins can only supply a few milliamps, far less than the hundreds
               of milliamps a motor typically requires.  ← CORRECT
            D) GPIO pins cannot change state fast enough for motor control.

        Q3. An H-bridge is used to control a DC motor. What does closing the two
            switches that direct current from left to right through the motor do?
            A) Brakes the motor by short-circuiting it.
            B) Spins the motor in one direction.  ← CORRECT
